A||||5||72vinman||What Glue should I Use??||||5||
Z||000000||72vinman||10-13-2001||10:30 PM||||I am in the process of redoing my interior. I just spent an hour removing the old material from the bottom of the door panel. That stuff was on there good. What type of glue was used. It is yellow and is very elastic. I am changing the material and would like to put a glue that is as good as the old one. <BR>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wolfhound||10-13-2001||11:43 PM|||| Use any good Contact Cement. Coat both surfaces.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-14-2001||12:01 AM||||I second that motion.  If you clean the surface you're gluing well, contact cement works great.  Just as long as your material has a backing that won't allow the glue to soak through, you'll be fine.  Beware if you aren't using a backed material though, as it will soak through.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||gt boy||10-14-2001||12:19 AM||||vinman...sounds like your winter project just got an early start!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||10-14-2001||01:05 AM||||I use Three-M  Yellow weatherstrip adhesive<BR>You can get it at nearly all auto stores. I got mine at Advance Auto. This sounds like what was on it. Anyway it is good stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000005||72vinman||10-14-2001||01:03 PM||||Thanks for the tips guys. I will look into both types.<BR>GT Boy, Yes I did get an early start. I had put the panels in the basement to make room in the garage. So while I was watching the hockey game I figured I would keep myself busy. If the weather clears up I will go out and take some pics of the dash. I have already done the carbon fiber on the dash plates. It came out really good.||||reg||10
